+# Superseded Phase 9 evaluation artifacts — DO NOT USE
+
+These files predate `experiments/phase9_regen_clean_csv.py` and contain
+scores from the contaminated original Phase 9 run. They are retained only
+for provenance and are **not** read by any final pipeline.
+
+The authoritative Phase 9 artifacts are:
+  - experiments/results/phase9/evaluation_results.csv   (5,522 rows, clean)
+  - experiments/results/phase9/evaluation_summary.json  (regenerated)
+
+| Archived file | Why superseded |
+|---|---|
+| evaluation_pump.csv.bak | Pre-repair; contains 8 zero-metric rows from an aborted `--smoke-test` run. |
+| evaluation_pump_repaired.csv | Step-8 repair keyed on filename alone; MIMII reuses filenames across `normal/` and `abnormal/`, so 3 normal rows received the abnormal recording's score. |
+| evaluation_summary.json.bak | Summary computed from the above. |
+| evaluation_{fan,pump,slider,valve}.csv | Stale per-type outputs of the original run. Their AUCs (0.698577 / 0.863535 / 0.881314 / 0.828308) are the SUPERSEDED values; the clean values are 0.698489 / 0.865713 / 0.884086 / 0.833465. |
+
+Clean per-machine-type metrics come from
+`experiments/results/phase11/per_type_summary.json`.
+
+Historical scripts `phase9_step7_root_cause.py`, `phase9_step8_repair.py`
+and `phase9_cross_machine_analysis.py` reference some of these paths. They
+are historical and are not part of the final pipeline.
